      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a decent start, but to be honest, the \"urgency\" feels a little thin. I'm worried if we send this, it'll just blend in with all the other nonprofit emails they get. \n\nOur internal review team uses that keyword score we talked about to make sure we're actually being impactful. In this draft, the score is pretty low. We really need to dial up the impact to ensure donors feel the gravity of the situation. \n\nCan you try again? Try to integrate more of those key terms (save, urgent, help, protect, crisis, immediate) so the message carries more weight. I'm still stressing: don't lose the professional tone or make it a list of words, but we definitely need a more 'high-signal' version that hits those points more frequently.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
